# Vulnerabilities that are knowingly accepted, one ID per line.
#
# Only add an entry with a reason that explains why the vulnerable code cannot
# be reached from this binary. scripts/govulncheck.sh fails on every other
# finding, and warns when an entry here is no longer reported so the list does
# not rot.

# Both advisories are daemon-side Moby bugs: an AuthZ plugin bypass on
# oversized request bodies (4887) and an off-by-one in plugin privilege
# validation (4883). This project only links the Docker *client* and only ever
# calls ContainerList, Events and Ping - it never runs a daemon, never installs
# a plugin and never uses AuthZ plugins.
#
# They are flagged because the fix landed in github.com/moby/moby/v2 >= 2.0.0-beta.8
# and the advisory lists no fixed version for the github.com/docker/docker
# +incompatible line we depend on. govulncheck therefore treats the whole
# module as vulnerable, so every client symbol we touch reports as "called".
#
# Remove these once the client is migrated to github.com/moby/moby/v2 (that
# module is still in beta; see the roadmap).
GO-2026-4887
GO-2026-4883
